// SPOT R1.6.5.1 — Global API surface for automation & testing
//
// 2026-05-03 R1.6.5.1 — JSX-side cosmetic hotfix for D-149 caught by Cowork closure
//   verification (parallel to D-133 sweep guardrail). Top-left version badge at L5436
//   was emitting literal "R1.6.4" string when in Developer mode (estimatorMode===false),
//   while __SPOT_UI_VERSION constant + tab title + server /api/health were all on
//   R1.6.5. One-site bump to "R1.6.5.1" to mark the catch-up. No behavioral change.
//   Engine, server, calibration UNCHANGED.
//
// 2026-05-03 R1.6.5 — JSX-side fixes for D-143 + D-145 ship:
//   D-143: Discard button in parse-review modal now clears parseResult + parseFieldChecks
//          (was: only setParseModalOpen(false), which left stale parseResult in state and made
//           "Build Estimate" button incorrectly read as "Review Build" cache-hit. Single-site
//           edit at the modal Discard button.)
//   D-145: Parse-review modal layout restructured so Build All / Build Selected / Discard
//          buttons are ALWAYS reachable, regardless of how many BOM components or asks the
//          parse returned. Previously, Multi-Part summary + asks list grew unbounded inside
//          the modal flex column, pushing the footer below the maxHeight:92vh clip line and
//          making the action bar unreachable on long parses (e.g. L'Oreal 17-PDF / 10-comp /
//          13-ask response). Fix: wrapped Multi-Part summary + Asks + Toolbar + Diff table
//          in ONE scrollable container (flex:1 overflowY:auto minHeight:0); added
//          flexShrink:0 to header and footer so they stay pinned; capped Asks list at 28vh
//          internal scroll so a long ask list doesn't crowd everything else; truncated long
//          fileList in footer (>60 chars) so the Files span doesn't wrap the action button
//          group offscreen.
// 2026-05-02 R1.6.4 — Global API surface for automation & testing
// 2026-05-02 D-139 (R1.6.4): Build Estimate button cache-aware dispatch. When parseResult
//   exists, click reopens review modal instead of re-firing /est/parse-rfq. Fixes duplicate-parse
//   429 rate_limit_error cascade (450k input tokens/min cap) caught on L'Oreal 379-8596 multi-PDF
//   folder. Label flips to "Review Build" when cached. Pairs with server D-141 token-budget
//   pre-flight (defense in depth). See DEV_D139_Design_Decision.md.
// 2026-05-02 D-141 (R1.6.4): /est/parser-budget poller appends ?clientKeyPresent=1 when any
//   wf_anthropic_key_* exists in localStorage. Server uses this to report `configured: true` +
//   `keySource: "client (browser)"` when no server-side .env key is set. Stops the badge from
//   lying that the parser is unconfigured when a working browser key is in play.
// 2026-05-01 D-136 (R1.6.3): Parser UX rename + knowledge-aware extraction. "Parse RFQ" → "Build Estimate"
//   cascade across 15 sites; modal title, action buttons (Build All / Build Selected / Discard), status
//   row ("Last build:") all updated. Server-side knowledge injection comprehensive (canonical terms,
//   quoting rules, board library, route eligibility, customer codes, control table defaults, harness
//   M1-M5 derivation) — server changes paired in spot_server.js. Closure gate TC-D136 sub-cases (1)-(5).
// 2026-05-01 D-137 (R1.6.3): Em-dash JSX-text-content escape bug at L8849 modal sub-header (same class
//   as D-132 \u00B7 fix). Wrapped \u2014 in JSX expression {"\u2014"} so Babel emits "\xE2\x80\x94"
//   string arg to React.createElement instead of literal 6-char "\u2014" text.
// 2026-05-01 D-134 (R1.6.2): RFQ folder orphan fix. Watches archiveFolderName transitions
//   from TBD-prefixed → real-customer-prefixed and POSTs /archive/rename to preserve files.
//   On rename success, refetches /archive/list to update the drop-zone tile + paperclip badge.
//   On 409/503/network failure, surfaces a toast and leaves files orphaned (degraded but visible).
// 2026-04-30 D-124: Cost-aware route selection — autoRoute = cheapest viable route.
//                   Replaces D-121 hard-preference Bobst-first early-return. Shared
//                   evaluateRoutes helper unifies routing logic between autoRoute and
//                   compareRoutes (eliminates Crest custom-vs-stock sub-bug). Fleet
//                   regression: pre-D-124 fleet Δ +32.05% R² -0.55 → post-D-124 fleet
//                   Δ +6.55% R² 0.84, restoring D-110 calibration. UI flag label renamed
//                   "Bobst auto-route eligibility". See DEV_D124_Design_Decision.md.
// 2026-04-30 D-133: Two surviving "R1.5.10" string literals at L3132 (browser tab
//                   title builder) and L5249 (EST/version badge in header) bumped
//                   to "R1.5.11.2". Pure string fix — engine, runner, server, schema
//                   unchanged. R1.5.11.1 header bump caught L4/L11 but missed both
//                   live-emit sites. See DEV_D133_Design_Decision.md for guardrail.
// 2026-04-29 D-132: RFQ Parser diff modal — wrap \u00B7 escapes in JSX expressions
//                   ({"\u00B7"}) at L5218/L8701/L8703/L8750. Babel does not interpret
//                   JS unicode escapes inside JSX text content. Cosmetic only.
// 2026-04-28 D-131: applyParsedFields populates bomItems[] when Multi-Part RFQ parsed.
//                   Auto-apply confidence threshold lowered to 0.75 for Multi-Part (vs 0.85 Simple).
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
window.__SPOT_UI_VERSION = "R1.6.5.1";
window.__SPOT_SESSION_LOG = [];
window.__SPOT_LOG_EVENT = function(event) {
  const entry = { ts: Date.now(), event };
  window.__SPOT_SESSION_LOG.push(entry);
  return entry;
};

